{"id": "EUVD-2026-103773", "enisaUuid": "bb5f47e9-d5f5-3b96-9b0e-624c4769c331", "description": "In the Linux kernel, the following vulnerability has been resolved:\n\nmtd: core: call _get_device() with the master MTD\n\n__get_mtd_device() calls the master's _get_device() callback with mtd,\nwhich may be a partition. __put_mtd_device() passes the master.\n\nThis breaks gluebi partitions because gluebi_get_device() uses\ncontainer_of() and therefore requires the master MTD. Pass the master\nto _get_device(), matching _put_device().", "datePublished": "2026-10-18T15:49:42", "dateUpdated": "2026-10-21T12:57:19", "baseScore": 0.0, "references": ["https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/d94731cafa57e2c986ff391122d1494e5a3f3c3f", "https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/95c8f36293c22d450c371167ad4f9a5bbadc7539", "https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/f971f1c63cf71579258360a12bd185bc1cd1a043", "https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/dc482a281a19a7d7e91ad1b2d551bb301c54d0e6", "https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/12b31d1acd20b3185bb5f0748db0cf6874c8e9d1"], "aliases": ["GHSA-p7f7-33cf-6r2w", "CVE-2026-98833"], "assigner": "Linux", "epss": 0.17, "enisaIdProduct": [{"id": "1653cd4e-0c32-3ba2-aad0-8ae9f2e86acc", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "46b5889cc2c54bac7d7e727a44d28a298df23cef <d94731cafa57e2c986ff391122d1494e5a3f3c3f"}, {"id": "254adb87-e720-3bd3-8621-4d689d262d29", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "patch: 0"}, {"id": "55b7bfc6-dd91-324b-aaa8-3d213b01071f", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "46b5889cc2c54bac7d7e727a44d28a298df23cef <12b31d1acd20b3185bb5f0748db0cf6874c8e9d1"}, {"id": "5fca2b52-f18b-343e-aba4-33c516b881c8", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "patch: 6.18.56"}, {"id": "62e2c58e-1525-30ea-8517-df656a9c0396", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "patch: 6.12.113"}, {"id": "636